From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000066 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: branch stub after restore

The physical direct-stub image rewrites both pt_regs EPC and ErrorEPC to the
copied KSEG0 stub before the final return, but the retained post-restore
header still shows that the stub never executes. The direct branch added for
the original /init EPC only matches 0x004002f0, so after rewriting the saved
EPC to 0x80401000 it skips itself and falls back to the unreliable eret path.

Accept either the original /init EPC or the copied stub EPC in the post
RESTORE_SOME branch and jump directly to the copied stub. This keeps the final
device path out of the problematic eret handoff while still allowing the stub
to clear ERL and alias the userspace stack before entering /init.
---
 arch/mips/kernel/entry.S | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/entry.S
@@ -154,8 +154,12 @@ restore_partial:		# restore partial frame
 	 nop
 	LONG_L	k1, PT_EPC(sp)
 	li	k0, 0x004002f0
-	bne	k1, k0, 1f
+	beq	k1, k0, 2f
+	 nop
+	li	k0, 0x80401000
+	bne	k1, k0, 1f
 	 nop
+2:
 	lui	k0, 0xa13f
 	li	k1, 0x51510007
 	sw	k1, 20(k0)
-- 
2.45.0
